From 267dd0fd2f30b56b8e23275d6e3ed5a54cb79359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pablo vela <pablovela5620@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:57:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add OPENCV_FISHEYE camera model support to Caspar GPU bundle
 adjustment

Follows the OPENCV pattern of upstream PR #4611.  OPENCV_FISHEYE has the same
parameter arity (2 focal + 2 principal point + 4 extra = 8), so it reuses the
V8 merged-calib / V6 split focal_and_extra node layout that #4611 showed fits
the 48 KB shared-memory budget; the shared-memory objection raised in issue
#4371 targets 12-param THIN_PRISM_FISHEYE and does not apply here.

caspar_generate.py (+161):
  - OpenCVFisheye{Pose,Calib,PrincipalPoint,FocalAndExtra} node types and
    their Const twins, plus ConstOpenCVFisheyeSensorFromRig.
  - opencv_fisheye_core: the Kannala-Brandt residual, transcribed from
    OpenCVFisheyeCameraModel in sensor/models.h (FisheyeFromNormal o
    Distortion o ImgFromFisheye).  models.h guards theta/r with
    'if (r > epsilon)'; a branch does not survive symbolic codegen, so the
    core uses Matrix.norm(sf.epsilon()) = sqrt(r^2 + eps), which has the same
    r -> 0 limit.
  - opencv_fisheye_split_core, the two FIXABLE tables, and merged + split
    register_camera_model calls.

generated/{f32,f64} (+448 files): BOTH precision trees regenerated, unlike
#4611 which shipped f32 only and would not compile with CASPAR_USE_DOUBLE=ON.
Only the 224 new per-model files and the four aggregate files
(solver.{h,cc}, caspar_mappings.{h,cu}) change per tree; every pre-existing
kernel is byte-identical, so PINHOLE and SIMPLE_RADIAL cannot regress.

caspar_model_adapter.h (+~460): OpenCVFisheyeAdapter with
FocalAndExtraSize()==6, PrincipalPointSize()==2, CalibSize()==8, the
15-variant SetVariantFactors switch, 17 new CasparSolverSizing fields, the
factory case, and the CreateSolver positional-argument surgery.  Both
argument orders were read off the generated GraphSolver constructor in
generated/f32/solver.h rather than inferred: OpenCVFisheye* sorts before
Pinhole*, so all pre-existing node-count arguments shift by four.

bundle_adjustment_caspar.cc (+10): pose-pool and calib sizing hookup.
doc/faq.rst: supported-model list.
